# swordcheck: optional API keys
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (next to where you run the tool) or to
# `~/.swordcheck/.env`, and fill in what you have. Everything is optional:
# the tool works without any key. A variable set in the shell wins over this
# file. Never commit `.env`; it is in .gitignore.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env

# --- NVD (National Vulnerability Database) ---------------------------------
# Used by: --vulns --online, for macOS, apps and Homebrew formulae.
# Without a key the NVD allows 5 requests per 30 seconds, so the tool waits
# 6.5 s between products. With a key it allows 50 per 30 seconds and the tool
# waits 0.7 s: about ten times faster on the first run of the day.
# Free, by e-mail: https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/request-an-api-key
NVD_API_KEY=

# --- Services that need no key ----------------------------------------------
# These are also queried with --online. They have no key and no account, so
# there is nothing to set here:
#   OSV.dev   (dependency advisories, npm malware)  https://osv.dev
#   CISA KEV  (known-exploited catalog)             https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog
#   EPSS      (exploit probability)                 https://www.first.org/epss
